# Context7 Usage
RULE: When working with any external library, add `use context7` to your prompt to fetch current docs via the Context7 MCP server.
WHY: Training data may be outdated; Context7 fetches live, version-accurate docs for the library in use.
DO: Add `use context7` whenever using FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Redis, Pydantic, httpx, or any third-party package.
NEVER: Rely on training-data knowledge alone for external library APIs — always fetch with Context7.
EXAMPLE: "How do I configure async sessions in SQLAlchemy? use context7"
